The product of fractions is found by multiplying the numerators together and multiplying the denominators together.
So, the product of one-half, two-thirds, and three-fourths is $\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)=\frac{1\cdot 2\cdot 3}{2\cdot 3\cdot 4}=\frac{6}{24}=\boxed{\frac{1}{4}}$.
