The function $f$ is defined on positive integers as follows:
\[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n + 10 & \text{if $n < 10$}, \\
f(n - 5) & \text{if $n \ge 10$}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find the maximum value of the function.

solution_steps:
Substituting the coordinates of the points into the equation $y = ax + b$, we get the system of equations \[
\begin{aligned} 5 &= 4a + b \\ 17 &= 8a + b \end{aligned}
\] Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get $12 = 4a$, so $a = 3$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get $5 = 4(3) + b$, so $b = -7$. Therefore, $a - b = 3 - (-7) = \boxed{10}$. The answer is: 10

Let $x=0.4\overline{5}$. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 10 gives $10x=4.\overline{5}$. Subtracting the first equation from the second gives $10x-x=4.\overline{5}-0.\overline{5}$, or $9x=4.1$.
Multiplying both sides of this equation by $\frac{1}{9}$ gives $x=\frac{4.1}{9}=\boxed{\frac{41}{90}}$.
The answer is: \frac{41}{90}

We know that $\binom{n}{k}=\binom{n-1}{k-1}+\binom{n-1}{k}$.
Using this identity, we can find $\binom{24}{4}$ and $\binom{24}{5}$:
\begin{align*}
\binom{24}{4} &= \binom{23}{3} + \binom{23}{4} = 1771 + 8855 = 10626, \\
\binom{24}{5} &= \binom{23}{4} + \binom{23}{5} = 8855 + 33649 = 42504.
\end{align*}
Now, we can find $\binom{25}{5}$:
\begin{align*}
\binom{25}{5} &= \binom{24}{4} + \binom{24}{5} = 10626 + 42504 = \boxed{53130}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 53130

