solution_steps:
Using the product-to-sum identities, we have
\begin{align*}
\cos x + \cos 3x + \cos 7x + \cos 9x &= (2\cos^2 x - 1) + (4\cos^3 x - 3\cos x) + (2\cos^2 3x - 1) + (4\cos^3 3x - 3\cos 3x) \\
&= 6\cos^3 x + 4\cos^3 3x + 2\cos^2 x + 2\cos^2 3x - 6\cos x - 3\cos 3x.
\end{align*}
This expression can be written as $a \cos bx \cos cx \cos dx$ if we let $a = 6$, $b = 1$, $c = 3$, and $d = 3$. Therefore, $a + b + c + d = 6 + 1 + 3 + 3 = \boxed{13}$.The answer is: 13

